# Pi-hole Custom DNS — /etc/pihole/custom.list
#
# This file shows the local DNS A records added by 07-pihole-dns-records.sh.
# Format: <IP>  <hostname>
#
# Copy to /etc/pihole/custom.list on your Pi-hole LXC (CT101), then reload:
#   pihole restartdns reload
#
# Replace "yourname-lab.com" with your actual registered domain.
#
# DNS resolution flow:
#   Internal hosts   → resolved directly from this file
#   AD domain (corp) → forwarded to Samba DC at 10.10.10.3 (see 09-pihole-conditional-forward.sh)
#   All other DNS    → forwarded upstream to Cloudflare 1.1.1.1

# Management network
192.168.1.100  proxmox.yourname-lab.com

# Internal network (vmbr2 — 10.10.10.0/24)
10.10.10.1     edge.yourname-lab.com
10.10.10.2     pihole.yourname-lab.com
10.10.10.3     dc01.corp.yourname-lab.com
10.10.10.10    admin-internal.yourname-lab.com
